1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,180
You wake up in Mira's bed.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,070
Four hours from your own.

3
00:00:05,090 --> 00:00:05,820
Her phone.

4
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:07,005
Her flat.

5
00:00:07,025 --> 00:00:09,675
Her alarm, which is a song you hate.

6
00:00:09,964 --> 00:00:12,190
For one day, you're living her life.

7
00:00:12,214 --> 00:00:13,985
And she's living yours.

8
00:00:14,005 --> 00:00:16,035
Everyone else thinks this is completely

9
00:00:16,055 --> 00:00:17,130
normal.

10
00:00:17,419 --> 00:00:19,270
The swap ends at midnight.

11
00:00:22,321 --> 00:00:23,951
Your brother is eating cereal out of

12
00:00:23,971 --> 00:00:24,580
a pan.

13
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:26,272
We don't have clean bowls.

14
00:00:26,292 --> 00:00:27,569
Why do you live like this?

15
00:00:27,589 --> 00:00:29,346
What's on your calendar today?

16
00:00:29,366 --> 00:00:29,841
Oh.

17
00:00:29,871 --> 00:00:30,701
Ten o'clock.

18
00:00:30,721 --> 00:00:31,881
Group presentation.

19
00:00:31,901 --> 00:00:32,996
Urban drainage.

20
00:00:33,016 --> 00:00:34,399
Slide four is yours.

21
00:00:34,419 --> 00:00:35,984
What's on slide four?

22
00:00:36,004 --> 00:00:36,864
Drainage.

23
00:00:36,884 --> 00:00:39,088
I don't know anything about drainage.

24
00:00:39,108 --> 00:00:40,108
Nobody does.

25
00:00:40,128 --> 00:00:41,483
That's why it's a course.

26
00:00:41,503 --> 00:00:43,033
Also, I'm going to your work.

27
00:00:43,053 --> 00:00:44,178
What do you do all day?

28
00:00:44,198 --> 00:00:45,033
Emails.

29
00:00:45,053 --> 00:00:47,155
Mostly emails about other emails.

30
00:00:47,175 --> 00:00:48,113
Oh no.

31
00:00:49,163 --> 00:00:51,143
Her course mates are lovely.

32
00:00:51,163 --> 00:00:53,268
They call you Mira, hand you a coffee

33
00:00:53,288 --> 00:00:55,100
and ask you about drains.

34
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:56,725
You ready, Mira?

35
00:00:56,745 --> 00:00:57,299
So ready.

36
00:00:57,319 --> 00:00:57,975
Born ready.

37
00:00:57,995 --> 00:00:58,852
Drains.

38
00:00:59,903 --> 00:01:01,608
Slide four is a pipe.

39
00:01:01,628 --> 00:01:03,708
You talk about the pipe for three minutes.

40
00:01:03,728 --> 00:01:06,050
You say "flow" eleven times.

41
00:01:06,070 --> 00:01:06,870
Unusual.

42
00:01:06,890 --> 00:01:07,660
Passionate.

43
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:08,435
Mostly wrong.

44
00:01:08,455 --> 00:01:09,336
B minus.

45
00:01:09,356 --> 00:01:11,401
That's her best mark yet.

46
00:01:11,551 --> 00:01:13,527
You decide not to tell her.

47
00:01:14,437 --> 00:01:16,732
Your boss asked me how my weekend was,

48
00:01:16,752 --> 00:01:18,582
and then he listened to the answer.

49
00:01:18,602 --> 00:01:19,387
Is he okay?

50
00:01:19,407 --> 00:01:20,232
That's new.

51
00:01:20,252 --> 00:01:21,746
He's been listening lately.

52
00:01:21,766 --> 00:01:23,446
Also, I did all your emails.

53
00:01:23,466 --> 00:01:24,600
It took forty minutes.

54
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:26,270
That's three weeks of emails.

55
00:01:26,290 --> 00:01:27,310
You're welcome.

56
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:30,715
Her phone never stops.

57
00:01:30,735 --> 00:01:31,530
Her mum.

58
00:01:31,550 --> 00:01:32,805
Her flatmates.

59
00:01:32,825 --> 00:01:34,980
A group called "Course Panic".

60
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,080
People ask her things all day, and she

61
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:38,845
answers every one of them.

62
00:01:38,865 --> 00:01:40,620
You get a strange feeling.

63
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,666
You know her better than anyone.

64
00:01:42,691 --> 00:01:44,746
And you have never seen how tired she

65
00:01:44,766 --> 00:01:45,333
is.

66
00:01:46,322 --> 00:01:48,702
Her flatmates knock for pizza night.

67
00:01:48,722 --> 00:01:50,732
They're kind, and they're funny, and

68
00:01:50,752 --> 00:01:53,107
they don't know that she hates olives.

69
00:01:53,127 --> 00:01:55,412
You pick the olives off without thinking.

70
00:01:55,432 --> 00:01:57,761
How did you know she hates olives?

71
00:01:57,781 --> 00:01:58,904
Lucky guess.

72
00:01:59,704 --> 00:02:00,239
Hey.

73
00:02:00,259 --> 00:02:01,567
Can I ask you something?

74
00:02:01,587 --> 00:02:02,248
Sure.

75
00:02:02,268 --> 00:02:03,848
I needed your phone to check the train

76
00:02:03,868 --> 00:02:04,648
times.

77
00:02:04,668 --> 00:02:06,033
And I found your drafts.

78
00:02:06,983 --> 00:02:08,138
Your drafts.

79
00:02:08,158 --> 00:02:10,238
Forty messages you started, to her,

80
00:02:10,258 --> 00:02:12,192
over two years, and never sent.

81
00:02:12,212 --> 00:02:14,092
"I'm proud of you." "I miss you being

82
00:02:14,112 --> 00:02:15,992
two minutes away." "Your new flat is

83
00:02:16,012 --> 00:02:17,557
small and I love it."

84
00:02:17,577 --> 00:02:19,125
Why didn't you send any of these?

85
00:02:19,625 --> 00:02:21,155
I didn't want to bother you.

86
00:02:21,175 --> 00:02:22,764
You've got a whole new life.

87
00:02:22,784 --> 00:02:24,264
You're in my whole new life.

88
00:02:24,284 --> 00:02:26,076
You're the person I tell things to.

89
00:02:28,026 --> 00:02:29,719
Ten minutes to midnight.

90
00:02:29,739 --> 00:02:30,490
Send them.

91
00:02:30,510 --> 00:02:31,474
All of them?

92
00:02:31,494 --> 00:02:32,339
All forty.

93
00:02:32,359 --> 00:02:33,689
Before we swap back.

94
00:02:33,709 --> 00:02:35,555
I want to get them on my own phone.

95
00:02:36,605 --> 00:02:38,660
You hit send forty times.

96
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:40,810
Her phone buzzes forty times in your

97
00:02:40,830 --> 00:02:43,335
hand, which is a very strange way to

98
00:02:43,355 --> 00:02:44,502
receive a hug.

99
00:02:44,522 --> 00:02:46,652
Number twelve is just the word "sandwich".

100
00:02:46,672 --> 00:02:48,027
That was a whole day.

101
00:02:48,047 --> 00:02:49,410
You'd know if you'd been there.

102
00:02:49,430 --> 00:02:51,360
I'm sending you one back for every single

103
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:51,873
one.

104
00:02:52,923 --> 00:02:54,478
At midnight, you wake up in your own

105
00:02:54,498 --> 00:02:55,153
bed.

106
00:02:55,173 --> 00:02:56,503
Theo's snoring.

107
00:02:56,523 --> 00:02:58,138
There's a pan in the sink.

108
00:02:59,048 --> 00:02:59,943
Read them all.

109
00:02:59,963 --> 00:03:01,127
Sending you forty back.

110
00:03:01,147 --> 00:03:02,202
Pace yourself.

111
00:03:03,252 --> 00:03:05,399
Your phone buzzes forty times.

112
00:03:05,989 --> 00:03:07,560
You read every one.

113
00:03:09,950 --> 00:03:11,405
What would your best friend find in

114
00:03:11,425 --> 00:03:12,442
your drafts?
